    "sub_ename": "ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING FUNDAMENTALS I",
    "describe_ch": "This course covers the fundamental concepts and applications of electric/electronic circuits for electrical and computer engineers as well as for engineers who need to gain a broad understanding of this field. The course starts with basic concepts, including charge, current, voltage, and resistive circuits. Essential concepts, devices, theorems, and dc circuits, first-order circuits, and ac circuits will be discussed subsequently. Also discussed are basic electronic components including diodes and transistors and their primary applications.",
